<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramiro II of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 898–951</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramiro II was king of León from 931 to 951. In 939 he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-simancas">Battle of Simancas</a>, one of the greatest Christian victories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>, and pushed the frontier south to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tormes">Tormes</a>. He also contended with the ambitions of Fernán González, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, who gradually made his county independent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramiro-ii-of-leon.jpg" alt="Ramiro II of León" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramiro2Leon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
